1
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,519
I'll take you somewhere with me.

2
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,199
- Where?
- Skull Island.

3
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,239
What?

4
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,600
Win is dead.

5
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,560
You're very brave to come back here.

6
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,320
Our substitutes have arrived.

7
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,679
If we want to leave this island,

8
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,200
we have to kill them.

9
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:16,960
Let's go.

10
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,840
Sairung.

11
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,680
It's time I took revenge.

12
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:40,760
‎Pat? You're dead?

13
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:49,720
Pat.

14
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,480
How are you doing this?

15
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:58,960
Hatred and vengeance.

16
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:04,080
Prawin, we have to kill them.

17
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,399
After everything that's happened,

18
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,320
none of you thought to tell me?

19
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,119
Everything happened so fast
that no one had time to think.

20
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:32,560
No one meant to keep
anything from you, Mr. Mek.

21
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,280
It was my fault.

22
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:39,040
I wanted to go to Skull Island
even though Na tried to stop me.

23
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:43,320
I'm sorry about your brother.

24
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,400
But I don't agree
with risking your lives by going there.

25
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:50,039
If you ask me,

26
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:53,759
the only way
to help Prawin's spirit find peace

27
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:56,560
is to make merit for him.

28
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,440
I agree.

29
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:02,239
Since everyone's here together,

30
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:05,479
why don't we make merit and offer food
at Mr. Thongdee's temple tomorrow?

31
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:08,400
How about that?
I'll take care of the food.

32
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,360
Thank you so much.

33
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,839
Then tonight, Da can stay with Mook,

34
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:24,959
and Mr. Narathon can stay in my room.

35
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,040
Wait.

36
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:31,280
Narathon has a house. He can stay there.

37
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:39,680
I'm sure Mr. Narathon understands. Right?

38
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,880
I understand.

39
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,319
It'll be much more convenient
if he stays here.

40
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:50,359
We still need
to plan tomorrow's merit-making.

41
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:54,160
Mr. Narathon and Na will have to
drive me to the market in the morning.

42
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,160
Dear,

43
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,160
offering food to all the monks isn't easy.

44
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:11,639
I'd better return to the temple.

45
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:13,400
I need to let everyone there prepare.

46
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,640
I'll take you.

47
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,440
Thank you.

48
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:37,040
You can't escape me, Sairung.

49
00:06:56,040 --> 00:07:00,120
You have to become my substitute.

50
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:07,280
I'm scared. Please don't hurt me.

51
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:09,360
I'm scared.

52
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,440
Pat, kill her.

53
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,080
There's no way
you can get off this island.

54
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:16,080
You have to become my substitute.

55
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:25,400
You! Die now!

56
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:34,799
Pat!

57
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,560
Pat!

58
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,880
Ms. Sairung, let's go.

59
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:09,440
Come on.

60
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:20,520
I never thought you'd leave the monkhood.

61
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:22,800
It's such a shame.

62
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:25,560
Good monks like you are hard to find.

63
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:33,360
There are many monks
better than I ever was.

64
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,120
I may not

65
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,200
be as good as you think.

66
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,640
That's not true. I've known you for years.

67
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:48,160
You've always done good deeds
and taught people many valuable lessons.

68
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:52,239
I still follow your teachings

69
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,240
to this day.

70
00:09:58,440 --> 00:09:59,520
In that case,

71
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:04,040
may I say something about Narathon?

72
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:08,720
Of course.

73
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:11,840
I've known Mr. Narathon
for a long time as well.

74
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:17,960
He's a kind-hearted young man
who's compassionate

75
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:19,560
and selfless.

76
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,080
People like him are rare.

77
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,840
If you let him slip away,

78
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,160
it would be a real shame.

79
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,080
Thank you for bringing me back.

80
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,080
It was my pleasure.

81
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,200
Let's go, Kliang.

82
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,960
Gold. My gold.

83
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,879
What about my gold?

84
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:42,000
Do you believe me now?
That island really is haunted.

85
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,760
Even if it is, we can deal with it.

86
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,160
What I don't understand is

87
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:51,280
how Pat ended up dying there.

88
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,120
She probably came after the gold,
just like we did.

89
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:01,200
Which means there must be
other ghosts on that island.

90
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:05,520
I don't think we should ever go back.

91
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:08,320
We were lucky to make it out alive today.

92
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,720
Please don't do anything to me.

93
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,520
Don't kill me.

94
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:11,560
Of course not.

95
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,480
I can't kill you two.

96
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,960
You're already dead.

97
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,280
Dead?

98
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:26,240
How is that possible?

99
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:30,920
It's not true, is it?

100
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,520
It's not true.

101
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,640
Look carefully.

102
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:01,760
This is not true.

103
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:06,000
Don't be upset.

104
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:10,119
No matter what,

105
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,960
you'll stay on this island forever.

106
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,320
But if you agree to serve me,

107
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:17,999
maybe

108
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,760
I'll find you some substitutes.

109
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:25,920
But if not...

110
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:42,320
It's burning!

111
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,040
It's hot.

112
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,000
It's hot!

113
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,280
I think I'd better head home.

114
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:06,200
Okay. We can meet at the temple tomorrow.

115
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,960
Mr. Narathon was just about
to head back to the fish farm, Dad.

116
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,480
Is it inconvenient for you to stay here?

117
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:33,760
No, sir. It's just...

118
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:37,960
Then let him stay with Na,
just like your mom suggested.

119
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,520
I'm not dreaming, am I?

120
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:50,960
Ouch.

121
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,080
Why'd you pinch me?

122
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:55,720
So you'd know this is real.

123
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:00,240
Does this mean your father

124
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:03,080
is finally giving me the green light?

125
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:08,040
Don't celebrate just yet.
It's not exactly a green light.

126
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:12,040
That's okay.

127
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:14,440
This is good enough.

128
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:16,919
I'll prove myself

129
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:18,960
until he accepts me.

130
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,560
And what if you never succeed?

131
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:28,960
I believe time proves everything.

132
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,120
But you have to promise me something.

133
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,960
Promise what?

134
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:41,080
No matter how long it takes,

135
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,360
you'll wait for me.

136
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,960
I promise. I'll wait for you.

137
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:51,800
Only you.

138
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:15,520
Well, well.

139
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:19,599
Are you worried Mr. Narathon
is going to sneak into Mook's room?

140
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,519
I know he'd never do that.

141
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:26,480
Otherwise, I wouldn't have let him stay.

142
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:30,399
I'm glad

143
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:32,559
you're giving him a chance.

144
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:35,080
I think he's a good man.

145
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:39,400
I've known that for a long time.

146
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,520
And after what Venerable Sir...

147
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:48,120
I mean Mr. Thongdee said,
I'm even more certain.

148
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,000
Oh?

149
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:55,000
Then why are you still
worried about Mr. Narathon?

150
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,600
It's not Mr. Narathon I'm worried about.

151
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:08,679
When I took Mr. Thongdee
back to the temple,

152
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:09,840
I saw...

153
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:13,560
Saw what?

154
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,200
I saw him without a head.

155
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,560
What?

156
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,320
There's an old saying that
if you see someone without a head,

157
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:27,360
their death is near.

158
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:30,280
I've heard that too.

159
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:32,760
That's why I'm worried.

160
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:35,120
I'm afraid something terrible
is going to happen to him.

161
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,640
Maybe your eyes
were just playing tricks on you.

162
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:44,000
Don't overthink it.

163
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:47,880
Mr. Thongdee is loved
and respected by everyone.

164
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:50,399
Anyone who'd wish him harm

165
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,120
doesn't deserve to be called human.

166
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:19,120
The moment I've been waiting for
has finally arrived.

167
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,680
Fate itself is on my side.

168
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,120
Son,

169
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:33,719
prepare the island.

170
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:36,520
Make it worthy of welcoming my bride.

171
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:08,960
Win...

172
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:13,360
Win.

173
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:20,599
Da.

174
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,000
Win!

175
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,960
Did you dream about him again?

176
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:33,040
Yes.

177
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:36,040
But it was strange.

178
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:38,880
How?

179
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:45,120
He wasn't frightening this time
like I saw before.

180
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:47,360
There wasn't any blood.

181
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,560
He didn't ask me to help him.

182
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:55,720
It was like he came to say goodbye.

183
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:05,200
Maybe he's finally found
a way off the island.

184
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:09,800
I don't know.

185
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:12,120
But I hope so.

186
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:17,479
Let's ask Mr. Thongdee tomorrow.

187
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:19,440
He might know the answer.

188
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:26,880
Get some sleep. We have to wake up early.

189
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:39,680
Wait.

190
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,120
Where are you going?

191
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:46,560
I'm going downstairs for some water.
Want me to bring you some?

192
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:50,160
No, thanks.

193
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:43,080
‎Mr. Narathon?

194
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:06,640
Mr. Narathon, what are you doing here?

195
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:25,120
Who are you?

196
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:38,880
I am the one you love.

197
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:43,840
The one I love...

198
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:46,840
That's right.

199
00:23:52,360 --> 00:23:53,600
We're leaving together.

200
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:58,840
Yes.

201
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:01,200
We're leaving together.

202
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:34,800
It's so beautiful.

203
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:40,920
I'm glad you like it.

204
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:46,240
I love it.

205
00:24:58,600 --> 00:25:00,120
We're going to get married

206
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:04,160
and live together on this island forever.

207
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:09,000
Yes.

208
00:25:23,080 --> 00:25:25,080
I'm sorry I'm late.

209
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:27,280
That's okay.

210
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:31,240
Where's Kaimook?
I thought she'd come down with you.

211
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:34,080
She wasn't in the room.

212
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:38,600
Maybe she went for a walk on the beach.

213
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:41,440
But it's still so early.

214
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:45,720
I'll go look for her.

215
00:25:46,280 --> 00:25:48,520
I'm coming with you.

216
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:49,960
Let's go.

217
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:06,800
I really saw it.

218
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:10,559
Maybe you were seeing things.

219
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:13,600
No, I wasn't. There's no way.

220
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:16,920
I heard rumors about the ghost ship.

221
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,440
But I actually saw it
with my own eyes last night.

222
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:24,880
Just talking about it
still gives me goosebumps.

223
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:27,559
What did it look like?

224
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:29,720
It was a huge ship.

225
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,960
But the moment I stared at it,

226
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:35,360
it disappeared into the darkness.

227
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:38,000
It had to be the ghost ship.

228
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,639
Then why did it come back to shore?

229
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:43,120
How should I know?

230
00:26:43,840 --> 00:26:47,080
But I swear I really saw it.

231
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,680
What?

232
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:57,960
You mean that ghost took Mook again?

233
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:00,559
Oh,

234
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:01,960
my poor daughter.

235
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:06,520
How could it come
all the way to our house?

236
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:08,200
I'm going to Skull Island.

237
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:11,080
Calm down, Mr. Narathon.

238
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,160
I can't.

239
00:27:13,960 --> 00:27:15,400
I'm worried about Kaimook.

240
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:19,320
That ghost must have taken her.

241
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:25,000
We're all worried about Kaimook.

242
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:27,520
But we have to keep our heads.

243
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:30,439
I agree with Na.

244
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:32,599
We're only assuming.

245
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:35,680
Mook just disappeared at the same time
the villagers saw the ghost ship.

246
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:39,280
She might not be there at all.

247
00:27:40,040 --> 00:27:43,200
There is one person
who can give us the answer.

248
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:04,560
Is Kaimook on Skull Island?

249
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:08,880
Don't worry.

250
00:28:09,760 --> 00:28:11,520
Kaimook isn't in any danger.

251
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:15,920
The reason he took her
isn't the same as the others.

252
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:19,320
We still have time
to figure out how to save her.

253
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:24,160
But if we rush there now...

254
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:26,920
not only will we fail,

255
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:29,200
everyone will die.

256
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:36,200
What should we do, Na?

257
00:28:37,840 --> 00:28:38,880
Mook.

258
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:49,559
Good morning, Ms. Su.

259
00:28:49,560 --> 00:28:51,879
Good morning, Mr. Phum.

260
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:54,120
I thought you'd be taking
another two or three days off.

261
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:57,759
Ms. Pakarang, are you fully recovered?

262
00:28:57,760 --> 00:28:59,080
- Yes.
- Good.

263
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:01,679
Do I have
a lot of urgent paperwork waiting?

264
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:04,599
Not just a lot, Mr. Phum.

265
00:29:04,600 --> 00:29:06,240
A mountain of it.

266
00:29:07,760 --> 00:29:10,319
Help me sign. Do you have a signature?

267
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:11,399
You have to sign it yourself.

268
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:12,840
- It's alright.
- Kathy?

269
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,759
What are you doing?

270
00:29:25,760 --> 00:29:28,479
Mr. Phum, please don't.

271
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:31,560
He's Ms. Pakarang's fiancé.

272
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:48,719
Thank you

273
00:29:48,720 --> 00:29:51,360
for saving my fiancée, Kathy,
after her accident.

274
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:55,200
Kathy?

275
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:58,640
Yes, she's my fiancée.

276
00:29:59,800 --> 00:30:02,200
Both of her parents died.

277
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:06,000
After that, we got engaged
and planned to get married.

278
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:19,120
Mom, who's that foreigner?

279
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:23,720
He is...

280
00:30:28,440 --> 00:30:31,239
Ms. Su, please take Kang to wait outside.

281
00:30:31,240 --> 00:30:32,560
Yes, sir. Let's go.

282
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:40,080
I know everything from Mr. Alan now.

283
00:30:40,760 --> 00:30:42,999
Your name is Kathy.

284
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:46,319
You came to Thailand
because Mr. Alan cheated on you.

285
00:30:46,320 --> 00:30:48,040
He had another woman.

286
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:51,280
Please talk to him.

287
00:31:02,200 --> 00:31:03,400
Kathy.

288
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:07,040
Don't worry.
I'm not here to interfere with your life.

289
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:10,120
I only came to apologize

290
00:31:11,320 --> 00:31:12,720
for hurting you.

291
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,560
I'm really sorry.

292
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:25,880
But I couldn't abandon my responsibility.

293
00:31:27,120 --> 00:31:28,960
I'm sorry for betraying you.

294
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:37,520
Can you forgive me?

295
00:31:52,560 --> 00:31:53,480
Yes.

296
00:31:55,240 --> 00:31:56,440
I forgive you.

297
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:06,320
Thank you.

298
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:12,760
Thank you so much.

299
00:32:31,320 --> 00:32:34,440
Actually, Alan's a good man.

300
00:32:35,160 --> 00:32:36,040
Yes.

301
00:32:36,880 --> 00:32:40,360
I believe that
if Ms. Kathy were still alive,

302
00:32:41,360 --> 00:32:44,560
she would've forgiven him
just as I did.

303
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:50,959
Let's go get something to eat.

304
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:54,960
I'll invite Thon too.
I want to ask him more about Skull Island.

305
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:57,120
You're going to help my father?

306
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:59,879
I need to know more information first.

307
00:32:59,880 --> 00:33:01,800
Thon probably knows more than anyone.

308
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:10,400
Hello, Thon? Where are you?

309
00:33:13,840 --> 00:33:15,359
Don't do anything yet.

310
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:16,800
Wait until I get there.

311
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:19,999
What happened?

312
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:21,519
Kaimook has disappeared.

313
00:33:21,520 --> 00:33:24,240
They think that mad ghost
took her to Skull Island.

314
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:13,960
You're awake, Kaimook?

315
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:16,000
Yes.

316
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:37,120
Did you sleep well?

317
00:34:37,719 --> 00:34:38,800
Yes.

318
00:34:45,560 --> 00:34:47,718
Why aren't any of my family

319
00:34:47,719 --> 00:34:50,159
or friends here for our wedding?

320
00:34:52,440 --> 00:34:53,520
They are.

321
00:34:55,080 --> 00:34:56,120
You have an older sister.

322
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:00,600
Where is she now?

323
00:35:07,400 --> 00:35:11,240
She's busy preparing for
our wedding tonight.

324
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,120
I'd like to meet my sister.

325
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:19,640
Of course.

326
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:51,920
Just give in and serve him.

327
00:35:52,720 --> 00:35:54,600
It has to be better
than suffering like this.

328
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:59,640
I'll never serve anyone.

329
00:36:01,720 --> 00:36:03,880
Then do you have any way
to escape this island?

330
00:36:08,480 --> 00:36:09,640
Now I finally understand

331
00:36:10,480 --> 00:36:12,640
why Sarai hated us so much.

332
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:17,120
Being trapped here...

333
00:36:18,640 --> 00:36:20,440
is torture.

334
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,600
I can't take this anymore.

335
00:36:25,680 --> 00:36:27,680
Why are you talking about Sarai?

336
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:30,280
Stop complaining and figure out a way out.

337
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:44,600
No!

338
00:36:45,160 --> 00:36:46,280
I'm not going.

339
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:48,280
I'm not going.

340
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:50,239
I'm not going.

341
00:36:50,240 --> 00:36:52,559
- Sairung.
- I'm not going.

342
00:36:52,560 --> 00:36:53,560
Sairung.

343
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:58,560
Ms. Sairung?

344
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:00,240
Where did you go?

345
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:15,480
You!

346
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:25,079
If you still refuse to become my servant,

347
00:37:25,080 --> 00:37:28,480
you will suffer
more pain than you can imagine.

348
00:37:37,400 --> 00:37:41,240
I surrender.

349
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:53,960
Kaimook.

350
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:02,320
Kaimook?

351
00:38:13,680 --> 00:38:16,200
This is your older sister, Sairung.

352
00:38:29,080 --> 00:38:30,720
Why can't I remember her?

353
00:38:32,200 --> 00:38:35,040
Why doesn't she feel familiar?

354
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:41,920
Kaimook.

355
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:45,600
Sairung...

356
00:38:46,360 --> 00:38:47,720
is your older sister.

357
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:55,320
Sairung is my older sister.

358
00:38:58,840 --> 00:39:00,200
That's right.

359
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:05,520
I'm so happy to finally meet you.

360
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:13,280
Sairung,

361
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:15,640
take good care of Kaimook.

362
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:19,160
Yes.

363
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:32,560
Sairung.

364
00:39:35,240 --> 00:39:36,400
Yes, it's me.

365
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:54,960
This island feels familiar.

366
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:58,240
But I can't remember when I've been here.

367
00:39:59,760 --> 00:40:01,000
And it feels like

368
00:40:01,520 --> 00:40:03,120
there's something stuck in my head.

369
00:40:04,280 --> 00:40:05,520
But I can't remember it.

370
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:09,640
Whenever I try too hard to remember,
my head starts to hurt.

371
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:22,760
Do you remember someone named Narathon?

372
00:40:25,040 --> 00:40:26,240
Narathon?

373
00:40:30,560 --> 00:40:31,959
Who is he?

374
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:33,880
He's the person you love.

375
00:40:36,480 --> 00:40:38,800
Isn't Mr. Men the one I love?

376
00:40:40,360 --> 00:40:43,520
That evil ghost must've put you
under a spell, Kaimook.

377
00:40:45,640 --> 00:40:47,680
What are you talking about?
I don't understand.

378
00:40:49,480 --> 00:40:51,080
I'll tell you the truth.

379
00:40:52,240 --> 00:40:53,960
But you have to promise

380
00:40:54,680 --> 00:40:57,000
to help me in return.

381
00:40:58,080 --> 00:40:59,320
Deal?

382
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:10,200
What truth?

383
00:41:13,120 --> 00:41:14,839
Men isn't human.

384
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:17,959
He's a ghost. He brought you here

385
00:41:17,960 --> 00:41:19,920
because he's fallen for you.

386
00:41:26,240 --> 00:41:28,879
The one you love

387
00:41:28,880 --> 00:41:30,320
is Narathon,

388
00:41:30,920 --> 00:41:32,200
not Men.

389
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:44,640
Mr. Narathon.

390
00:41:50,360 --> 00:41:52,160
I told you the truth.

391
00:41:54,760 --> 00:41:57,080
Now it's your turn to help me.

392
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:00,720
Help what?

393
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:03,040
Let me kill you.

394
00:42:03,880 --> 00:42:06,040
So you can become my substitute.

395
00:42:08,480 --> 00:42:09,480
Sairung?

396
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:28,480
Kaimook.

397
00:42:30,880 --> 00:42:33,279
Who are you? How dare you hug me?

398
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:35,839
We promised we'd wait for each other.

399
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:37,720
Don't you remember, Kaimook?

400
00:42:41,040 --> 00:42:42,839
<i>If he's not afraid of dying,</i>

401
00:42:42,840 --> 00:42:44,639
<i>then let him die.</i>

402
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:46,519
This time, you'll never run away again.

403
00:42:46,520 --> 00:42:47,720
We'll see.

404
00:43:24,320 --> 00:43:25,800
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
